{"evidence":["Ran `cargo test -p tank_core --test conservation_regression -- --nocapture` in `/home/master/p/tank-simulation`: all 6 named conservation tests passed.","Ran `cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_conservation -- --nocapture` in `/home/master/p/tank-simulation`: the end-to-end runner reported 6 passed, 0 failed, and printed per-scenario delta magnitudes.","Reviewed `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/conservation_regression.rs`: all six required unit-test entry points exist with descriptive doc comments, and the file enables detail tracing for every scenario.","Reviewed `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_conservation.rs`: the harness runs all six scenarios in sequence and fails the test if any scenario returns `Err` or panics.","Reviewed `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/conservation_regression.rs:82-90` and `:441-665`: `dump_trace()` is only reached through `assert_conserved()`, while the trim/remove, trim/leave, and water-change unit tests use direct `assert!`/`assert_close()` paths."],"findings_or_gaps":["`/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/conservation_regression.rs:284` and `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_conservation.rs:319` only assert net conservation for the feeding scenario. They do not assert that the promised decomposition chain or microfauna-consumption path actually fires, so a regression that leaves feed stranded or disables one downstream stage while still conserving total mass would remain green.","`/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/conservation_regression.rs:375` only proves shrimp mortality occurred; it does not verify plant/algae senescence routing or a senescence-driven detritus increase. `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/conservation_regression.rs:619` and `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_conservation.rs:408` validate water-change nitrogen bookkeeping only, leaving carbon-side dilution/replacement mass balance unasserted.","The trace-artifact acceptance criterion is not fully met. Because `dump_trace()` is only wired through `assert_conserved()`, failures in `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/conservation_regression.rs:441`, `:504`, and `:619` will panic without writing the requested trace file."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Strengthen scenario 2 so it asserts the intended routing story, not just final totals: verify feed leaves particulate organics and reaches downstream pools or system deltas associated with decomposition, microfauna consumption, and nitrification.","Strengthen scenario 3 and scenario 6: add assertions that senescence-derived biomass reaches detritus, and validate expected carbon import/export and net carbon change for water changes in both the unit test and the e2e runner.","Refactor the open-system unit tests to use a shared 'dump trace before failing' helper so trim/remove, trim/leave, and water-change failures always emit the debugging artifact required by the bead.","After those changes, rerun `cargo test -p tank_core --test conservation_regression -- --nocapture` and `cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_conservation -- --nocapture` to confirm the tightened assertions still pass."],"outcome":"request_changes"}